part.section:
Enacted by Chapter 153, 2022 General Session2022Definitions.As used in this chapter:
"Commission" means the Cybersecurity Commission created in this chapter.
"Critical infrastructure" includes the following sectors the United States Department of Homeland Security identifies as critical:

chemical;
commercial facilities;
communications;
critical manufacturing;
dams;
defense industrial base;
emergency services;
energy;
financial services;
food and agriculture;
government facilities;
healthcare and public health;
information technology;
nuclear reactors, nuclear materials, and nuclear waste;
transportation systems; and
water and wastewater systems.
